# CPDV: checked against the text on bible.com, Sept 2026. The Catholic
# Public Domain Version is in the public domain, so its words are quoted.
use 3jn-1-14
use rev-20-8
use vulgate-verses

# Chapters whose last verse runs on through the next.
GEN 5:1-31 = GEN 5:1-31
2SA 13:1-38 = 2SA 13:1-38

# Exodus 39 gives the breastplate's fastenings in three verses, Hebrew
# 39:17-21, so it runs two behind, as DRC1752's does; 39:34 is "the veil, the
# ark, the bars, the propitiatory", mostly 39:35.
EXO 39:1-17 = EXO 39:1-17
EXO 39:18 = EXO 39:19
EXO 39:19 = EXO 39:21
EXO 39:20-25 = EXO 39:22-27
EXO 39:26 = EXO 39:28
EXO 39:27 = EXO 39:28
EXO 39:28-32 = EXO 39:29-33
EXO 39:33 = EXO 39:34
EXO 39:34 = EXO 39:35
EXO 39:35-36 = EXO 39:36-37
EXO 39:37 = EXO 39:38
EXO 39:38 = EXO 39:38
EXO 39:39-43 = EXO 39:39-43

# Esther in the Greek order: the Hebrew text in 3-5, 6:8-7:19, 9:17-12:12,
# 13:25-15:3. The Greek additions (Mordecai's dream, 1-2; the king's letters,
# 6:1-7 and 13:1-24; the prayers of Mordecai and Esther, 7:20-8:19; Esther
# before the king, 9:1-16; the dream explained, 15:4-14; and three lines
# inside 7) have no Hebrew verse. They go to Greek Esther (ESG), outside the
# synced books, so that, like Daniel 13-14 in vul.vrs, they pair with no
# other version's verse. Hebrew 4:12 has no verse: 7:14 opens with it.
EST 1:1-11 = ESG 1:1-11
EST 2:1-6 = ESG 2:1-6
EST 3:1-22 = EST 1:1-22
EST 4:1-23 = EST 2:1-23
EST 5:1-13 = EST 3:1-13
EST 6:1-7 = ESG 6:1-7
EST 6:8-9 = EST 3:14-15
EST 7:1-9 = EST 4:1-9
EST 7:10-11 = ESG 7:10-11
EST 7:12-13 = EST 4:10-11
EST 7:14-15 = EST 4:13-14
EST 7:16 = ESG 7:16
EST 7:17-19 = EST 4:15-17
EST 7:20-30 = ESG 7:20-30
EST 8:1-19 = ESG 8:1-19
EST 9:1-16 = ESG 9:1-16
EST 9:17-30 = EST 5:1-14
EST 10:1-14 = EST 6:1-14
EST 11:1-10 = EST 7:1-10
EST 12:1-12 = EST 8:1-12
EST 13:1-24 = ESG 13:1-24
EST 13:25-29 = EST 8:13-17
EST 14:1-32 = EST 9:1-32
EST 15:1-3 = EST 10:1-3
EST 15:4-14 = ESG 15:4-14

# The Canticle, divided more finely and without a title verse.
# 1:1 "Let him kiss me" and 1:2 split 1:2; 1:4-7 are the four clauses of
# "Draw me, we will run after thee"; 1:9-10 split 1:6.
SNG 1:1 = SNG 1:2
SNG 1:2 = SNG 1:2
SNG 1:3-4 = SNG 1:3-4
SNG 1:5 = SNG 1:4
SNG 1:6 = SNG 1:4
SNG 1:7 = SNG 1:4
SNG 1:8-9 = SNG 1:5-6
SNG 1:10 = SNG 1:6
SNG 1:11-21 = SNG 1:7-17
# 2:9-10 split "My beloved is like a roe" / "he standeth behind our wall",
# and 2:11-12 split "My beloved spake" / "Rise up, my love".
SNG 2:1-9 = SNG 2:1-9
SNG 2:10 = SNG 2:9
SNG 2:11 = SNG 2:10
SNG 2:12 = SNG 2:10
SNG 2:13-19 = SNG 2:11-17
# 5:1 "Let my beloved come into his garden" ends 4:16, and 5:19 "Where has
# your beloved gone" begins chapter 6, which runs one behind until 6:12
# "Return, return, O Sulamitess", the first half of Hebrew 7:1. Chapters 4
# and 7 are listed so that they and 5:1 and 6:12 map under one system.
SNG 4:1-16 = SNG 4:1-16
SNG 5:1 = SNG 4:16
SNG 5:2-3 = SNG 5:1-2
SNG 5:4 = SNG 5:2
SNG 5:5-18 = SNG 5:3-16
SNG 5:19 = SNG 6:1
SNG 6:1-11 = SNG 6:2-12
SNG 6:12 = SNG 7:1
SNG 7:1-14 = SNG 7:1-14
# 8:5-6 split "Who is this that cometh up from the wilderness" / "I raised
# thee up under the apple tree".
SNG 8:1-5 = SNG 8:1-5
SNG 8:6 = SNG 8:5
SNG 8:7-15 = SNG 8:6-14

# Isaiah 45:23-24 split "I have sworn by myself" / "every knee shall bow".
ISA 45:1-23 = ISA 45:1-23
ISA 45:24 = ISA 45:23
ISA 45:25-26 = ISA 45:24-25
# 2 Thessalonians 2:10 runs on through "God shall send them strong delusion"
# (2:10-11).
2TH 2:1-10 = 2TH 2:1-10
2TH 2:11-16 = 2TH 2:12-17
# Bel and the Dragon: 13:65, Astyages laid to rest, is already Bel 1:1, so
# 14:1 "Daniel was living with the king" is 1:2 and the chapter runs one
# ahead; 14:42, "Let all the inhabitants of the whole earth fear the God of
# Daniel", closes the last verse.
DAN 14:1-41 = BEL 1:2-42
DAN 14:42 = BEL 1:42

# Psalms, numbered as in the Vulgate (CPDV 15 is Hebrew 16).
# 13 (14): 13:4-6 are the lines Romans 3 quotes ("Their throat is an open
# sepulchre"), which the Hebrew lacks; they follow 14:3.
PSA 13:1-3 = PSA 14:1-3
PSA 13:4 = PSA 14:3
PSA 13:5 = PSA 14:3
PSA 13:6 = PSA 14:3
PSA 13:7-10 = PSA 14:4-7
# 15 (16): the last verse runs on through the next.
PSA 15:1-11 = PSA 16:1-11
# 71 (72), 99 (100): the title is a verse of its own, then "Give the king thy
# judgments, O God" and "Make a joyful noise unto the LORD".
PSA 71:1 = PSA 72:1
PSA 71:2 = PSA 72:1
PSA 71:3-20 = PSA 72:3-20
PSA 99:1 = PSA 100:1
PSA 99:2 = PSA 100:1
PSA 99:3-5 = PSA 100:3-5
# 92 (93): a title the Hebrew lacks, then 92:2-3 split "The LORD reigneth".
PSA 92:1 = PSA 93:1
PSA 92:2 = PSA 93:1
PSA 92:3 = PSA 93:1
PSA 92:4-7 = PSA 93:2-5
# 115 (116:10-19) and 147 (147:12-20), the Vulgate's second halves.
PSA 115:1-10 = PSA 116:10-19
PSA 147:1-9 = PSA 147:12-20
# 125 (126): 125:6-7 split "He that goeth forth and weepeth" / "shall doubtless
# come again with rejoicing".
PSA 125:1-6 = PSA 126:1-6
PSA 125:7 = PSA 126:6
# 135 (136): 135:27 repeats "Lord of lords" after the last verse.
PSA 135:1-26 = PSA 136:1-26
PSA 135:27 = PSA 136:26
